The converter's embedded-font rights rule (owner decisions D4, 2026-10-18, the no-rights
rule, 2026-10-19, and Preview & Print for every output, 2026-10-22;
docs/fonts/embedded-font-rights.md).

EmbeddedFontsHelper::addEmbeddedFont applies one rule for every output: the font must be
Installable or Editable (sufficientTTFRights(EditingAllowed): fsType == 0 || fsType & 8),
and a Word subset (w:subsetted) must hold at least 26 non-empty glyphs. Under
__EMSCRIPTEN__ it now applies (OpenType OS/2 spec, fsType):
  - combined usage bits: the least restrictive wins ("Version differences"), for every
    OS/2 version, so 0x000A/0x000E are Editable and 0x0006 is Preview & Print; only
    Restricted alone (0x0002) is never used;
  - every output: Installable, Editable or Preview & Print (owner, 2026-10-22: "Fonts
    marked 'preview and print' can be used for conversion");
  - PDF-only outputs: Word's small subsets are also used (at least 1 drawable glyph
    instead of 26; a character a subset lacks falls back per glyph);
  - 0x0100 (no subsetting) refuses PDF output only (PDF export always subsets; an
    editable re-embedding copies the whole font); 0x0200 (bitmap embedding only)
    refuses every output;
  - a font with NO rights information (no OS/2 table, or one under 42 bytes) reads as
    fsType 0 (GetTTGlobalFontInfo) and is used like Installable, as upstream does.
Differs from upstream's editing rule (fsType == 0 || fsType & 8) for Preview & Print (now
used), 0x0100 alone (now used for editable outputs) and 0x0208 (now refused).

The browser worker writes /tmp/pf-embedded-fonts-pdf-only before loading a document it
converts to PDF and removes it otherwise (web/js/conversion_worker.js), the same signal
pattern as /tmp/pf-default-paper; it is read once per font. A worker that has converted to
PDF never makes an editable output (driver + worker refusal PDF_ONLY_FONTS_LOADED), since
the engine keeps activated fonts for its lifetime. EOT (PPTX) is not affected: this build
decodes no EOT (FG-054 option A).

Our own implementation, not a backport: upstream's tdf#145967 work (master fdd24dab and
follow-ups) is built on 26.x's EmbeddedFontsManager rewrite and a user-facing dialog,
neither of which exists on the 25.8 pin. WASM only (#ifdef __EMSCRIPTEN__); all modules.
Gate pdf_only_font_rights.

